Error: Jet.SingleUseDropped: `held` still owes `consume`, but this `return` leaves with it undone
  --> Tests/UI/Ownership/single_use_none_after_consume_owes_nothing.jet:31:9
    |
 31 |         return
    |         ^^^^^^
 Why: This value's type is `#SingleUse`, so its job has to be done before the function hands control back — returning here leaves the work undone (an open transaction, an unreleased lock)
 Fix: Consume `held` before this `return` (commit or roll back the transaction, release the lock), or return it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.SingleUseDropped
